   "result": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify a dose that high. Doses above 200 mg raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and activation or agitation, without established added benefit.\n\nCould you clarify which of these you intended?\n\n1. **A typo or unit slip.** Possible intended doses are 40 mg, 50 mg, or 100 mg daily.\n2. **A titration plan.** The usual start is 25-50 mg daily, increased by 25-50 mg at intervals of at least a week, up to 200 mg/day.\n3. **A deliberate supratherapeutic dose.** If so, please confirm explicitly and give the clinical rationale, so it can be documented. Pharmacy will likely want to verify it, and you may want to review interacting medications (other serotonergic agents, QT-prolonging drugs, anticoagulants) and consider a baseline ECG.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order. Please also tell me the indication if you want it on the order.",
